claim.claim-text:
identifying one or more traits, said traits being one or more physiological, behavioural or biological states of the user that are potentially relevant to the wellness goals;
identifying one or more genetic factors of the user that are relevant to one or more of the traits;
identifying one or more environmental factors of the user that are relevant to said one or more of the traits;
assigning a weighting to each genetic and/or environmental factor for the traits, said weighting defining the likely effect that the genetic and environmental factors have on the traits;
calculating a trait score for each trait based on the weightings assigned to each trait, each trait score indicative of the likely biological, behavioural or physiological response of the user to the trait;
defining a trait profile for the user from the trait scores, said trait profile characterizing the user's likely biological, behavioural or physiological response to a wellness regime;
determining, based at least partly on the trait profile, a wellness regime that is optimised to the wellness goals of the user.
